n0.text:
{vessel} {CRASHED|WENT DOWN|GOT SMASHED} ON {ground}, {BROADCASTIN' A DEAD DISTRESS SIGNAL|BLEEDIN' STATIC INTO DA COMMS|RUNNIN' A BUSTED BEACON} EVERY {FEW|MANY} SECONDS.
{DA AIRLOCK IZ POPPED, DA REACTOR IZ DEAD COLD, BUT SOMETINK INSIDE IZ STILL DRAWIN' POWER.|REACTOR'S DEAD COLD, LIFE SUPPORT IZ GONE, BUT SOME IDIOT LEFT DA BEACON ON.|DA HULL IZ BREACHED AN' FREEZIN', BUT INTERNAL POWER IZ STILL HUMMIN'.}
{EITHER IT IZ AUTOMATED JUNK OR A REAL OBVIOUS TRAP.|LOOKS LIKE FREE SALVAGE, IF YOU NO MIND DA RADIATION.|NOBODY CAME TA HELP DEM, BUT WE MIGHT AS WELL LOOT DA CORPSE.}
DA BEACON HAB BIN {REWIRED|MOVED|TAKEN OFF DA BUS} AN' GIVEN A CELL OF ITS OWN!

{ZERO SOLID GROUND ANYWHERE.|NO LANDIN' ZONES IN SIGHT.|NUTTIN' BUT THICK, CHURNIN' ATMOSPHERIC LAYERS.} DA SIGNAL COMES FROM A FIXED DEPTH IN {place}, {ANCHORED DEAD STILL IN AN ATMOSPHERE DAT SHOULD CRUSH STEEL|HOLDIN' STATION AGAINST ALL LOGIC|HOVERIN' IN DA MIDDLE OF A TOXIC CLOUD BANK}.
{IT IZ EITHER AN AUTOMATED RELAY STATION OR SOMEONE REAL STUBBORN.|YOU IZ GOING TA HAB TA DIVE RIGHT INTO DA SOUP TA CHECK IT OUT.|DESCENDIN' INTO DAT SOUP IZ DEFINITELY GOING TA VOID DA HULL WARRANTY.}
IT HAB BIN AT DAT EXACT DEPTH FOR AS LONG AS DA SURVEY HAB RECORDS, THROUGH {FOUR|FIVE} STORM SEASONS DAT SHOULD HAB MOVED IT!

{A BELL IZ CLANGIN' OUT IN DA MIDDLE OF NOWHERE, {distance}, WHERE DA CHARTS SWEAR DERE IZ ONLY DEEP WATER.
THROUGH DA MIST YOU SPOT A RUSTED BUOY BOBBIN' AWKWARDLY IN DA SWELL. SOMEONE WELDED AN IRON LADDER ONTO DA SIDE AN' LITERALLY SPRAY-PAINTED A FAKE DOOR WIT A REAL HANDLE ONTO DA METAL.|DERE IZ A BUOY OUT HERE IN TWO HUNDRED METERS OF OPEN WATER, RINGIN' LIKE CRAZY. UP CLOSE, IT IZ A BEAT-UP RUSTED DRUM WIT A WELDED LADDER AN' A PAINTED DOOR DAT NO SHOULD BE DERE.|DERE IZ A BUOY OUT HERE IN FOUR HUNDRED METERS OF OPEN WATER, RINGIN' LIKE CRAZY. UP CLOSE, IT IZ A BEAT-UP RUSTED DRUM WIT A WELDED LADDER AN' A PAINTED DOOR DAT NO SHOULD BE DERE.}
DA BELL IZ RUNG BY DA SWELL AN' DA SWELL IZ NO BIG ENOUGH TA RING IT!

{A GLOWIN' TRANSLUCENT FIGURE IN A TWEED WAISTCOAT IZ FLOATIN' TWO FEET OFF DA GROUND IN DA RUINED COURTYARD.|DERE IZ AN ACTUAL GHOST HOVERIN' OVER DA RUBBLE, CLUTCHIN' A GLOWIN' GRIMORIE AN' MUTTERIN' TA HIMSELF.|A SPECTRAL CLERK IZ PACIN' DA CRACKED MARBLE FLOOR, FURIOUSLY STAMPIN' IMAGINARY PAPERS.}
{HE LOOKS UP, ADJUSTS GHOSTLY SPECTACLES, AN' DEMANDS TA SEE YA PERMITS.|HE SPOTS DA PARTY AN' IMMEDIATELY STARTS LISTIN' MUNICIPAL INFRACTIONS FROM TWO CENTURIES AGO.|HE YELLS DAT VISITIN' HOURS ENDED IN 1842 AN' THREATENS TA FINE YA ANCESTORS.}
DA SUMMONS IN ITS HAND IZ {COUNTERSIGNED|STAMPED TWICE|ENDORSED}, AN' ONE OF DA TWO HANDS DAT SIGNED IT IZ STILL WORKIN'!

{AN OVERGROWN CEMETERY ON DA HILL, PACKED WIT LEANIN' HEADSTONES AN' AGGRESSIVELY JUDGMENTAL STONE ANGELS.|A DREARY GRAVEYARD WHERE DA DEAD HAB BETTER REAL ESTATE DEN DA LIVIN'.|WEEDS AN' IVY IZ CHOKIN' A MASSIVE MARBLE TOMB IN DA CENTER OF DA GRAVEYARD.}
{DA IRON GATE TA DA MAIN MAUSOLEUM IZ SLIGHTLY AJAR, WIT FRESH FOOTPRINTS IN DA MOSS.|SOMEONE CLEARLY TRIED TA PRY DA HEAVY BRASS DOOR HANDLES OFF WIT A CROWBAR.|SENSORS DETECT HIGH MAGICAL RESONANCE AN' ZERO SIGNS OF RESPECT FOR DA DECEASED.}
DA CRATER IZ {NO NEW|WEATHERED|A YEAR OLD AT LEAST} AN' NUTTIN' HAB GROWN IN IT!

{SITTIN' ON A DUSTY SHELF IN DA VESTRY IZ A BUTCHERED ANOKI HANDSET WIT ITS CASIN' CRACKED OPEN.|DERE IZ AN ANOKI PHONE SITTIN' IN DA BACK OF DA VESTRY, HELD TOGETHER WIT ELECTRICAL TAPE.|ON A STONE LEDGE BEHIND DA ALTAR SITS AN ANOKI PHONE WIRED DIRECTLY INTO DA WALL.} {DA LEYLINE COIL HAB BIN RIPPED OUT AN' RE-SOLDERED BY AN AMATEUR.|SOMEONE CLEARLY JURY-RIGGED DA CHARGIN' CIRCUIT INTO DA STONE MASONRY.|DA BATTERY WAZ REMOVED YEARS AGO, BUT DA SCREEN IZ STILL GLOWIN'.}
{IT STARTS RINGIN' WIT AN ANNOYIN', CRACKED MECHANICAL BUZZ FROM INSIDE DA PLASTIC.|SUDDENLY DA DAMN TINK STARTS BUZZIN' WIT A TINNY, RUSTED BELL CHIME.|RIGHT ON CUE, IT RINGS WIT A HARSH, BROKEN RATTLE DAT MAKES YA TEETH ACHE.}
DA SOLDER ON DA WIRES IZ {FRESH|BRIGHT|NO OLD} AN' DA HANDSET HAB BIN IN DA VESTRY SINCE {timeAgo}!

c.text:
{DA PHONE BUZZES CONSTANTLY FOR A LONG STRETCH WHILE YOU TEAR DA VESTRY APART LOOKIN' FOR LOOT.|YOU IGNORE DA PERSISTENT RINGIN' AN' SYSTEMATICALLY RIFLE THROUGH EVERY DRAWER AN' CUPBOARD.}
{JACKPOT IN DA BACK CLOSET: AN ENCRYPTED GRIMORIE OF PHONE NUMBERS, A BOTTLE OF VINTAGE WINE, AN' A SEALED LOCKBOX.|YOU FIND FOUR CANDLES, AN UNOPENED BOTTLE OF COMMUNION LIQUOR, AN' A STACK OF VALUABLE NOTES.}
{AT LEAST DA ANNOYIN' RACKET DISTRACTED ANYONE FROM NOTICIN' YOU RANSACK DA PLACE.|FREE LOOT AN' VINTAGE BOOZE. WORTH DA HEADACHE.}

d.text:
{YOU CHUCK DA PHONE INTO DA BAPTISMAL FONT WIT A LOUD SPLASH. DA RINGIN' CUTS OUT INSTANTLY AN' DA ROOM TEMPERATURE DROPS TWENTY DEGREES.|YOU DROWN DA NOISY HANDSET IN HOLY WATER; IT SIZZLES, STEAMS, AN' GOES DEAD SILENT.}
{DA SCREEN IZ STILL LIT UNDER DA WATER, STUBBORNLY TICKIN' UP DA CALL DURATION IN NEON GREEN.|THROUGH DA MURKY WATER, DA SCREEN SHOWS DA CALL IZ STILL CONNECTED AN' RACKIN' UP LONG-DISTANCE FEES.}
{VATICAN AUTHORITIES WILL MAYBE-MAYBE SEND A COMMENDATION FOR DESTROYIN' UNSANCTIONED TECH, BUT YA FINGERS IZ NUMB FROM DA FROST.|DA PARISH WILL BE THRILLED YOU EXORCISED DEY PHONE, EVEN IF YOU RUINED DEY HOLY WATER.}

a1.text:
{YOU KEEP DEM TALKIN' FOR DA BEST PART OF AN HOUR WHILE DEY RAMBLE 'BOUT HISTORICAL GOSSIP, RATIONIN', AN' AN IMPENDIN' WAR.|DEY SPEND HALF AN HOUR VENTIN' 'BOUT GROCERY PRICES AN' POLITICAL DRAMA FROM DECADES AGO.}
{IN DA MIDDLE OF DA RANT, DEY CASUALLY DROP COORDINATES AN' DATES FOR AN UNDISCOVERED MILITARY CACHE.|RIGHT BEFORE HANGIN' UP, DEY LET SLIP DA LOCATION OF A FORGOTTEN EMERGENCY VAULT.|JACKPOT: DEY GAVE AWAY DA LOCATION OF AN OLD TREASURY DROP.}
{DA LINE GOES DEAD WIT A LOUD POP, AN' DA HANDSET FINALLY DIES FOR GOOD.|DA PHONE CLICKS, SPARKS ONCE, AN' BURNS OUT DA ANTENNA.|DA CONNECTION CUTS OUT, LEAVIN' YOU WIT VALUABLE INTEL AN' A FRIED PHONE.}

a2.text:
{YOU GIVE DEM DA CURRENT YEAR AN' DATE. DERE IZ A LONG, STUNNED SILENCE, FOLLOWED BY A DEFEATED GROAN ON DA LINE.|YOU BREAK DA NEWS 'BOUT WHAT YEAR IT IZ. DEY CURSE LOUDLY AT DA TEMPORAL DELAY.}
{DEY ASK YOU TA DELIVER A FINAL MESSAGE TA DEY OLD PARTNER WHO IZ NOW LIVIN' IN A RETIREMENT VILLAGE.|DEY BEG YOU TA PASS A MESSAGE TA AN ELDERLY CONTACT NEARBY.}
{YOU LOOK UP DA ADDRESS, DELIVER DA NEWS, AN' POCKET A SURPRISINGLY GENEROUS FINDER'S FEE.|A QUICK ERRAND, A FEW AWKWARD QUESTIONS, AN' AN EASY MORAL VICTORY.} {EVERYONE FEELS SLIGHTLY LESS CYNICAL FOR 'BOUT TEN MINUTES.|NO A BAD HAUL FOR PLAYIN' TEMPORAL RECEPTIONIST.}

b1.text:
{YOU DIAL DA SECOND NUMBER AN' AN OLD MAN ANSWERS ON DA FIRST RING: "SO SOMEONE FINALLY FOUND DA VESTRY RIG."|AN ELDERLY GUY PICKS UP IMMEDIATELY, ASKIN' IF YOU IZ CALLIN' FROM DA CHURCH.}
{TURNS OUT HE'S A RETIRED ENGINEER IN A CARE HOME IN {region}, DESPERATE TA GET HIS OLD PROTOTYPE BACK BEFORE HE KICKS DA BUCKET.|HE BUILT DA HACKED HANDSET FIFTY YEARS AGO AN' OFFERS HIS ENTIRE PENSION SAVINGS IF YOU BRING IT TA HIM.}
{EASY MONEY. YOU PACK DA CURSED PHONE INTO YA BAG AN' COLLECT DA BOUNTY.|HE PAYS UP IN CLEAN CASH WITOUT ASKIN' TOO MANY QUESTIONS.}

n0.text:
{IN DA DAMP BASEMENT BENEATH DA CASTLE, A HEAVY IRON VAULT DOOR IZ SEALED WIT THREE WAX CRESTS AN' AN OVERSIZED PADLOCK.|DOWN IN DA CASTLE CELLAR SITS AN ANCIENT IRON DOOR COVERED IN PEELIN' HERALDIC WAX.|DERE IZ A REINFORCED VAULT DOOR DOWN HERE DAT LOOKS LIKE IT NO HAB BIN OPENED SINCE DA MONARCHY COLLAPSED.}
{DA HINGES IZ RUSTED SOLID, BUT SOMEONE RECENTLY SCRATCHED A FRESH LINE OF WARDIN' RUNES ACROSS DA THRESHOLD.|DA LOCK HAB BIN PICKED TWICE, FAILED ONCE, AN' JAMMED WIT LEAD SOLDER.|SENSORS SHOW HIGH-VALUE LOOT INSIDE AN' A FIFTY PERCENT CHANCE OF ANCIENT CURSES.}
THREE CRESTS, AN' DA THIRD ONE IZ {NO A CREST ANYBODY CAN PLACE|FROM AN OFFICE DAT NEVER EXISTED|NEWER DEN DA OTHER TWO}!

{DEEP IN DA SWAMP, AN OLD WOODEN SHACK SITS ON ROTTIN' STILTS, SURROUNDED BY BUBBLIN' MUD AN' SWARMS OF BITIN' GNATS.|A MISERABLE SHACK IZ BALANCED OVER DA SWAMP WATER, SMELLIN' OF SULFUR AN' CHEAP TOBACCO.|OUT IN DA MUCK, A HERMIT'S CABIN IZ TIED TA THREE MANGROVE ROOTS WIT FRAYED ROPE.}
{AN OLD GUY IN RUBBER WADERS IZ SITTIN' ON DA PORCH, CLEANIN' A SHOTGUN AN' EYEIN' YA WALLET.|A SHIFTY SWAMP DRIFTER IZ WATCHIN' YOU THROUGH A CRACKED WINDOW, PRETENDIN' TA BE DEAF.|DA LOCAL HERMIT WAVES YOU OVER WIT A RUSTY MACHETE, LOOKIN' FOR A SUCKER TA TRADE WIT.}
DA SHACK IZ A LID. DA STILTS IZ {HOLDIN' IT DOWN|ANCHORIN' IT|STOPPIN' IT GOING ANYWHERE}!

{vessel} SITS AT {place} WIT DA RAMP DOWN AN' {cargo} HALF UNLOADED ONTO {ground}.
NOBODY IZ ABOARD. DA MANIFEST IZ ON A CLIP BY DA RAMP, FILLED IN PROPERLY ALL DA WAY TA DA THIRD PAGE, AN' DEN NO AT ALL.
DA THIRD PAGE ENDS MID-WORD. {RIGHT INSIDE DA WORD.|DA PEN STOPPED INSIDE A WORD.|SOMEBODY STOPPED WRITIN' BETWEEN ONE LETTER AN' DA NEXT.}
